{
  "note": "Every plate is the master with its paper ground removed by a border flood fill, cropped to the drawing, and written with a real alpha channel. The flood leaks through gaps in the crayon outline, so the paper it eats inside the drawing \u2014 the white page of an open notebook, the sheet under the spectacles \u2014 is put back afterwards: the transparency that the border cannot reach is enclosed by ink, and those pixels are given the master's own pixels. The transparent_fraction is measured on the file that ships; interior_holes is the transparency left over after the repair and is zero on every plate.",
